nouveau-vdec-probe.patch: nouveau winsys fix for upstream Mesa 17ca6174 on
pre-GSP chips under Linux nouveau, applied by
nvk/pascal/scripts/build-nak-nouveau.sh (the "NAK on nouveau" bundle, the
only build of this repo that compiles src/nouveau/winsys: nvk-macos.patch
leaves it out of the macOS dylib and of the patched Linux/sim tree, and the
pg106 backend sets cls_vdec = 0 / has_video = false itself).

nouveau_ws_device_new() probes for video decode by creating a VDEC context.
nouveau 1.4.3 (Linux 7.3) accepts the NVDEC channel on chips it runs without
GSP, GP106 included (runlist with the NVDEC engine), but nvkm's NVDEC engine
there has an empty sclass, so the channel's class list has no 0xb0 class.
nouveau_ws_video_context_init() passed oclass 0 to nouveau_ws_subchan_alloc(),
which asserts in any build with asserts on (debugoptimized): every program
died in vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices / NAK's hw_runner device open, before any
GPU work (GTX 1060 Mobile run 1, 2026-11-08; reproduced on drm-shim
nouveau_noop with NOUVEAU_CHIPSET=136). The context now fails with -ENODEV
when a requested class is missing, which leaves cls_vdec = 0 and
has_video = false as the probe intends. The two failure paths also free the
channel (and copy object) instead of leaking them.

Upstream main has the same code (checked 2026-11-08).

--- a/src/nouveau/winsys/nouveau_context.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/winsys/nouveau_context.c
@@ -228,10 +228,23 @@
 
    ret = nouveau_ws_context_query_classes(dev->fd, req.channel, classes);
    if (ret)
-      return ret;
+      goto fail_subchan;
 
    const uint32_t base = (0xbeef + req.channel) << 16;
 
+   /* nouveau (1.4.3+) hands out NVDEC channels on chips it drives without
+    * GSP, e.g. Pascal, but nvkm's NVDEC engine there exposes no class: the
+    * channel's class list has no 0xb0. That is no VDEC context; fail like
+    * a channel that could not be allocated instead of asserting below.
+    */
+   if (((engines & NOUVEAU_WS_ENGINE_COPY) &&
+        !nouveau_ws_context_find_class(classes, 0xb5)) ||
+       ((engines & NOUVEAU_WS_ENGINE_VDEC) &&
+        !nouveau_ws_context_find_class(classes, 0xb0))) {
+      ret = -ENODEV;
+      goto fail_subchan;
+   }
+
    if (engines & NOUVEAU_WS_ENGINE_COPY) {
       uint32_t obj_class = nouveau_ws_context_find_class(classes, 0xb5);
       ret = nouveau_ws_subchan_alloc(dev->fd, req.channel, 0,
@@ -254,6 +267,7 @@
 
 fail_subchan:
    nouveau_ws_subchan_dealloc(dev->fd, &ctx->vdec);
+   nouveau_ws_subchan_dealloc(dev->fd, &ctx->copy);
    nouveau_ws_channel_dealloc(dev->fd, req.channel);
 
    return ret;
